 ('@VehicleLayout','vehicle_layout_c01',['assets/asset_truck/truck_c02.png','assets/asset_riff/riff_c03.png','assets/asset_pip/pip_c01.png','assets/asset_driver/driver_c02.png'],'''Create ONE continuous ultrawide 21:9 spatial/scale reference of the truck immediately beside the clock tower at stormy night. Input 1 cream/red TRUCK DESIGN, input 2 Riff ONE complete otter, input 3 Pip ONE complete otter, input 4 ONE gray badger civilian driver. Exact scale: standing Riff and Pip each 1H; truck cab from road to roof 2H and total bumper-to-bumper length 5H. Put both brothers standing on the OPEN REAR CARGO DECK behind the cab, soles visibly on deck about 0.75H above road, low waist rail and crates behind them. The driver sits INSIDE cab behind its steering wheel, visible through cab glass, both hands on wheel, clearly different from Pip. Vehicle points right and occupies left/center of composition. Immediately ahead is a SHALLOW 18-20-degree ramp/loading bump; its tip is no more than 1.5H from the nearby tower entry window. Show ramp, truck and tower window together with a SHORT visible gap, not a distant tower. Tower facade fills right third, same painted brass/stone arched-window language. Beyond ramp, street visibly curves toward foreground/left around the tower so driver can turn truck away while rear-deck momentum sends brothers forward through nearby window. No launch yet: a single clear pre-action spatial setup, no multi-panel storyboard or time montage. All three actors remain in assigned compartments; no actor driving besides gray badger. Brass ray pistol stays in Riffs small right-hip holster. Same original 2D ink/cel character style, painted indigo/amber city, no numbers on visible clock faces, no captions, labels, arrows or text.''')
